{"at":"2026-11-26 18:55","message":"SUPABASE_DB_URL in .env still does not work. It starts with the password instead of 'postgresql://postgres:', and even with that fixed the direct host db.<ref>.supabase.co does not resolve from this machine (IPv4-only network, DNS ENOTFOUND). Do this: 1) Supabase dashboard > your project > Connect > choose 'Session pooler' (not Direct connection) and copy the full URI, which looks like postgresql://postgres.<ref>:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres. 2) Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the database password, URL-encoding special characters (+ is %2B, $ is %24, @ is %40), or reset it in Project Settings > Database to a simple letters-and-digits one (recommended, as the old one was printed in an agent log). 3) Put the whole string on the SUPABASE_DB_URL line of .env, with no spaces or trailing comment. 4) Re-run: node run_phases.mjs. Everything else in 01-setup is already done and passing."}